": "Alabama remains one of the most reliably Republican states in presidential politics, and the 2028 race opens without an incumbent after the term-limited president leaves office. The state's partisan lean of roughly fifteen points toward Republicans anchors the outlook, and recent primaries in which Trump-backed candidates prevailed underline the durability of that alignment. Neither party has settled on a nominee, and no general-election polls or expert ratings are yet available for this race.\n\nWith fundamentals doing the work, Alabama rates as Likely Republican, with a wide band of uncertainty reflecting the open field. A Democrat would need an unusually favorable national environment and a candidacy that runs far ahead of the state's normal lean to make this competitive. The biggest unknown is the identity of the nominees and how the national mood in 2028 settles, since neither is yet clear.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0488, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0924, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0912, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0912, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0824, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0837, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0865, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0895, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0869, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.087, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0756, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0829, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0893, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0877, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.078, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.0805, "margin": -15.0}]}